WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.590
So the Daily Show and the Colbert Report were
both responses to the Bush years. They were

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.960
about this alienation liberals felt from their
country at a moment when Fox News seemed the

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.190
authentic expression of the American psyche
and George W. Bush kept winning elections.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.890
But then what happened is that liberals began
winning elections. "Did you guys hear? It

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:25.630
looks like the Mets and the Tampa Bay Rays
are in -- they're in some trade talks. Oh! by

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:30.300
the way, did you guys hear about this?" The
constant crises of Obama's early presidency

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.300
gave the shows a lot to work with at first,
but as the Obama era quieted down, I think

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.820
it put the Daily Show and the Colbert Report
in a pretty strange position because Colbert

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.269
and Stewart became the voices of the dominant
political coalition. Punching Fox News kind

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:52.269
of became punching down. "Your distortions
and lack of fact footholds against mine. To

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.280
start us off, here's 50 of yours in a 6-second
Vine."

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.960
Their replacements -- Trevor Noah at

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:04.260
the Daily Show and Larry Wilmore in Colbert's
slot -- are both talented black comedians.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:10.250
They have a real skill for taking on America's
complicated, often really frustrating racial

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:17.750
politics. "Yeah I just flew in and boy are
my arms tired." "Ok, alright there, oldie

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:23.110
but a goodie. Very nice." "No, no seriously,
I've been holding my arms like this since

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:29.000
I got here." And so their takeover is a recognition
of one of the lessons of the Obama era, which

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.860
is that American politics isn't moving past
race. It's moving into it. This political

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.960
scientist at Brown University, a guy named
Michael Tesler, he goes and shows how in the

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:43.270
80s and 90s, when you polled racial controversies,
you didn't see a big partisan split. So the

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:47.920
number of Democrats who agreed with the O.J.
verdict was 50% and the number of Republicans

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.660
was 41%. But now you look at any controversy
that has even a hint of race in it, like say

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.670
the verdict with Zimmerman right, around Trayvon
Martin. 68% of Democrats were angry about

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:03.380
that. Only 20% of Republicans were angry about
it. There was a poll about whether 12 Years

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.259
a Slave should win an Oscar, and 53% of Democrats
thought it should and only 15% of Republicans

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:14.420
agreed. That isn't the kind of thing we've
seen the political parties splitting on before.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.310
Tesler's book, "Obama's race" describes an
inconvenient truth about the 2008 election:

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:24.439
It was the most racialized election in modern
American history. There's been no recent campaign

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:28.980
in which racial attitudes did as much to drive
political behavior and it's continued on.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.900
You even have racial differences in how much
people like Obama's dog. If you show people

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.599
a photo and you tell them it's Obama's dog,
folks who rank as having a little bit more

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:42.329
racial resentment, they tend to like that
dog less than if you show them the same dog

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:48.290
and tell them it's Ted Kennedy's dog. America
is sort of at the end of the Obama era, working

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:54.900
through its attitudes about race in a way
it sort of hasn't had to for a very very long

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.459
time. And you're seeing these shows try to
update for that. "I thought that Barack Obama

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:03.799
was post-racial." "Yeah. He is. We're not."

